#!/usr/bin/env deque
// An ant farm and nothing else: a screensaver. Run it: deque demo/antfarm.deque
//
// It begins with a queen alone, and it's kept: next time it's the same
// colony, older. deque demo/antfarm.deque --fresh begins again.
// i says how it's doing. f follows an ant. [ and ] slow and hurry its time.
// H is what's happened to it.
//
// v is the same colony from above. A click drops food. q q quits.
// Run it in two panes and press v in one: one colony, both views.
// Change the line under the --- for other ants: after `sky: ants` go any of
//   farm, ground · leafcutter, black, fire · soil, sand, gel · how many
// as in `sky: ants fire sand 90`.
cursor: off

---
sky: ants
